From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: v8-embed-feedstock <noreply@github.com>
Date: Tue, 2 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Hide the bundled ICU's symbols

The third file with this problem, after abseil.  v8.gyp compiles every V8
target with -fvisibility=hidden from its target_defaults;
tools/icu/icu-generic.gyp is a separate .gyp and inherits none of them, so
with --with-intl=small-icu the ICU compiled into the library exported its
entire API.  Measured on libv8.so.14.6.202.34: 9824 icu_78:: symbols plus
UCaseMap::, against 0 after this patch.

This is worse than the abseil case was.  ICU's icu_78 namespace protects
against mixing two different versions of ICU in one process; it does
nothing about two copies of the same version, which is exactly what an
embedder gets when the host already links ICU 78 -- as anything using Qt
does.  ICU also carries process-global state, the default locale,
converter caches and the data pointer among it, so interposition is not
merely an ODR technicality.

The flag works here because U_STATIC_IMPLEMENTATION is defined for these
targets, which makes U_EXPORT expand to nothing; there is no explicit
visibility attribute to override it.

The conditions are v8.gyp's target_defaults ones, verbatim.  After the
patch the library exports v8::, cppgc::, v8_inspector:: and weak std::
template instantiations, and nothing else -- 2743 symbols in total.

Not changed here, but noted: these targets are also compiled without
NDEBUG, so ICU's assert()s are live.  That is true of node's own builds
too and fixing it is a behaviour change this patch deliberately leaves
alone.
---
 tools/icu/icu-generic.gyp | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tools/icu/icu-generic.gyp b/tools/icu/icu-generic.gyp
--- a/tools/icu/icu-generic.gyp
+++ b/tools/icu/icu-generic.gyp
@@ -6,6 +6,26 @@
 
 
 {
+  # Same as v8.gyp's target_defaults.  This file is a separate .gyp and
+  # inherits none of them, which leaves every ICU target compiled at default
+  # visibility -- so a shared build of V8 with the bundled ICU exports ICU's
+  # entire API alongside its own.  U_STATIC_IMPLEMENTATION is defined here,
+  # so U_EXPORT is empty and nothing overrides the flag.
+  'target_defaults': {
+    'conditions': [
+      ['OS=="mac"', {
+        'xcode_settings': {
+          'GCC_SYMBOLS_PRIVATE_EXTERN': 'YES',  # -fvisibility=hidden
+          'GCC_INLINES_ARE_PRIVATE_EXTERN': 'YES',  # -fvisibility-inlines-hidden
+        },
+      }, '(OS!="aix" and OS!="os400") and (OS!="win" or clang==1)', {
+        'cflags': [
+          '-fvisibility=hidden',
+          '-fvisibility-inlines-hidden',
+        ],
+      }],
+    ],
+  },
   'variables': {
     'icu_src_derb': [
       '<(icu_path)/source/tools/genrb/derb.c',
